spec.section:
## 7. Handover gates for the author

Before marking this plan implemented, the author should produce a machine-readable CHD-3.3 manifest and verify:

- every `R32-001..027` appears exactly once in the new disposition register with status, exact changed paths, evidence requirement and remaining limitation;
- every `R31-001..030` remains present with its canonical disposition and R32 links;
- `D-039` is present in the decision register and in the authorization, archive, recovery, fixture and generated-register surfaces;
- every supported operation maps `operation → request/result schema → record/write → error → evidence query → recovery`;
- every cited path in the package manifest exists and its digest is recomputable from the delivered package;
- every restore statement resolves current permissions, while every fork statement preserves D-038's separate default/alternate/resync/no-auto-resync policy;
- no status field calls a specification-only artifact “implemented,” no fixture-only result “live,” and no planned scenario “run” without retained dated evidence;
- schema, example, table, figure source and generated output checks are run separately from visual rendering and owner acceptance.

Rendering is intentionally out of scope for this plan. The render/index ticket (T15/T16) may later perform visual QA, but no page count, PDF build, or image inspection is evidence for the contract corrections above.
